steps.diagnosis_json:
{"spec_element": "invariant",
 "proof_obligation": "preservation",
 "diagnosis": "The loop invariant 'forall i :: 1 <= i < (n) - 1 ==> a[i] == old(a[i-1])' is too weak. After each swap of a[0] and a[n], the element at position n receives old(a[n-1]) (from invariant 3), so when n is incremented, the new element at position n-1 satisfies a[n-1] == old(a[n-2]). But the invariant only covers i < n-1, not i = n-1, so Dafny cannot prove preservation. Changing the bound to '1 <= i < n' fixes both preservation and the postcondition (at exit n=a.Length, giving exactly the postcondition)."}

